(7515715, 1199804, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club! <br/> <br/>Very funny snapshot, love the expression on the faces of both dog and owner. Definitely meets the challenge criteria but the composition could have been a bit better as the dog and owner are kind of jammed into that left half of the pic.  No mention of what lens you used so don''t know if you could have zoomed out a bit to get the shot, then cropped the pic to make it more pleasing to the eye.  Otherwise exposure is fine, the subject matter cute and appealing and the backstory provided helps to explain the title.  Ah, women are so fickle! hehe<br/> <br/>Hope this critique has been of help, and feel free to PM me with any comments or questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  Very funny snapshot, love the expression on the faces of both dog and owner. Definitely meets the challenge criteria but the composition could have been a bit better as the dog and owner are kind of jammed into that left half of the pic.  No mention of what lens you used so don''t know if you could have zoomed out a bit to get the shot, then cropped the pic to make it more pleasing to the eye.  Otherwise exposure is fine, the subject matter cute and appealing and the backstory provided helps to explain the title.  Ah, women are so fickle! hehe Hope this critique has been of help, and feel free to PM me with any comments or questions, Susan', '2017-05-26 21:38:10.000000', NULL, 0),
